# Highland.js Parallel Tuple Sum

```javascript
const Highland = require('highland');

/**
 * Iterates over two sequences of 2-element tuples in parallel and appends
 * the element-wise sum of each tuple pair to a third sequence.
 * 
 * @param {Stream} stream1 - First stream of 2-element tuples [a, b]
 * @param {Stream} stream2 - Second stream of 2-element tuples [c, d]
 * @returns {Stream} Stream of summed tuples [(a+c), (b+d)]
 */
function parallelTupleSum(stream1, stream2) {
  return Highland.zip(stream1, stream2).map(([tuple1, tuple2]) => {
    const [a, b] = tuple1;
    const [c, d] = tuple2;
    return [a + c, b + d];
  });
}

// Example usage:
const stream1 = Highland([[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]]);
const stream2 = Highland([[10, 20], [30, 40], [50, 60]]);

parallelTupleSum(stream1, stream2)
  .each(result => {
    console.log(result);
  })
  .done(() => {
    console.log('Done!');
  });

// Output:
// [11, 22]
// [33, 44]
// [55, 66]
// Done!
```

## How it works:

1. **`Highland.zip(stream1, stream2)`** - Combines two streams in parallel, pairing elements at the same index from both streams
2. **`.map(([tuple1, tuple2]) => ...)`** - For each pair of tuples, destructures them and computes the element-wise sum
